  "routed": "docs/status/FINDINGS-FROM-AUTHORING.md F25",
  "reading": [
    "ENTITY-CBOR-ENCODING, before §1: \"The normative conformance contract for this specification is `Appendix",
    "E: Conformance Test Vectors`. An implementation of ECF is conformant iff it produces the required",
    "canonical bytes (and rejects the required non-canonical bytes) for every vector in the current published",
    "version of the appendix's fixture file.\" §E.6: \"Conformance reports MUST cite the corpus name and the",
    "sha256 of the `conformance-vectors.cbor` artifact\". The core floor row for fidelity says the mechanism is",
    "\"gated by that document's Appendix E\".",
    "",
    "THE CORPUS IS PINNED WITH THIS SNAPSHOT (completed 2026-09-12; see MANIFEST): 71 vectors — float 14, int",
    "14, length 8, map_keys 6, nested 6, primitive 6, tag_reject 5, content_hash 4, envelope 2, peer_id 3,",
    "signature 3.",
    "",
    "WHY NO WIRE SURFACE REACHES IT. An `encode_equal` vector gives an arbitrary `input` value — a float at an",
    "f16 boundary, an integer at 2^63 — and requires the encoder's bytes for it. A peer encodes only what the",
    "protocol causes it to emit; no core operation asks a peer to encode a caller-chosen value and return the",
    "bytes. ECP-R4's put/get round-trip reaches the DECODER and the relay path for such values, never the",
    "encoder's canonicalization of them (the caller supplies canonical bytes, and the peer preserves them).",
    "The `tag_reject` vectors DO have a wire proxy, and it is measured: `UNALLOCATED-cbor-tag-rejected`.",
    "",
    "WHAT THE SUITE CAN CHECK, AND DOES NOT CALL COVERAGE. Whether an implementation's conformance report",
    "cites this corpus by sha256 (§E.6). That is a check on the claim, not on the encoder."
  ],
