  "unreachable": {
    "class": "GUIDE-CONFORMANCE §5.2a — a pinned-input vector gate: the crossing is the shared file, not a live peer",
    "why_no_proxy": "encode_equal inputs are arbitrary values no core operation asks a peer to encode and return; the nearest wire path (tree put/get) returns the caller's own canonical bytes and cannot fail the way a non-canonical encoder fails. decode_reject's tag vectors have a proxy, measured separately; its other decode behaviours have no vectors to proxy.",
    "discharged_by": [
      "the implementation's own §E.3 harness over the pinned artifact, reported with (spec-version, corpus name, sha256) per §E.6",
      "a host-seam exposing the encoder, where a peer's harness offers one"
    ],
